WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.040
Bees have barbed stingers that can stay in the skin and continue pumping venom.

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.320
If stung by a bee, you should act quickly to get that stinger out as soon as possible.

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:11.860
Instead of pinching it, it is better to use the edge of a credit card

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:15.160
to scrape the stinger away in the opposite direction from how it went in.

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:19.480
Once the stinger is removed, you'll want to wash the area thoroughly with soap and water

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:22.500
and apply an ice pack to help manage the pain and swelling.

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:26.620
While you provide this care, your most critical task is to monitor the person

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:28.459
for any signs of an allergic reaction.

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:33.400
If you notice immediate red flags like trouble breathing or swelling of the face and throat,

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:36.840
you should use an epinephrine auto-injector if they have one prescribed

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.740
and call 911 immediately.

